### Conference and Staff Attorneys

The **Conference Attorneys**, who have offices on the first floor of the Cuyahoga County Court House, conduct the Appellate Court's Prehearing Conference Program established in 1991. The program is designed to settle civil cases before the parties in pending appeals incur the expense and time required to bring the dispute to oral argument and judicial decision.

The **Staff Attorneys**, who have offices of the second floor of the Cuyahoga County Court House, conduct legal research, prepare legal memoranda, assist the Judges on a wide range of legal subjects, and respond to inquiries by attorneys and litigants on court procedure.

Expand all Collapse all

### Conference Attorneys

[Mary Pat Horwitz, Administrative Counsel and Conference Attorney](javascript:void(0))

Ms. Horwitz has been with the court since 1993. She received her B.A. in English from Hiram College where she was inducted into the Phi Beta Kappa Honor Society. She obtained her law degree from the Franklin Thomas Backus School of Law at Case Western Reserve University. Following her admission to the Bar, she served as a judicial attorney for Judge James M. Porter until 2000, Judge Colleen Conway Cooney until 2003, and Judge Patricia Ann Blackmon until 2016. In addition to serving as the court’s administrative counsel, Ms. Horwitz handles mediations for the court as part of the Appellate Court’s Prehearing Conference Program.

[Newton S. Cargill, Mediator and Conference Attorney](javascript:void(0))

Mr. Cargill received a Bachelor of Arts degree in economics from Howard University and then worked in the financial-planning industry for 15 years before obtaining his law degree from Cleveland-Marshall College of Law. Following admission to the bar in 2001, Mr. Cargill served as a public defender with the Legal Aid Society of Cleveland’s then Criminal Division.

Mr. Cargill first joined the court in 2003, where he has been privileged to serve as a Judicial Attorney for three judges, namely: Honorable Patricia Ann Blackmon, Honorable Mary Eileen Kilbane, and the Honorable Emanuella D. Groves. Additionally, in between his judicial clerkships, Mr. Cargill served as Manager of three divisions of the Cuyahoga County Clerk of Courts and as the Court Administrator of the Cleveland Municipal Court’s Housing Division.

In December 2022, Mr. Cargill was appointed to the position of Mediator and Conference Attorney. He has received specialized training in mediation and negotiation sponsored by the Supreme Court of Ohio.

