### Staff Attorneys

[Toni Querry Farkas, Staff Attorney](javascript:void(0))

Toni joined the Eighth District Court of Appeals in 2012. She received her B.A. from Cornell University and graduated summa cum laude from Cornell Law School in 1996. Toni served as a judicial attorney for the Honorable Kenneth Rocco and the Honorable Eileen A. Gallagher before assuming her current role as one of the court’s staff attorneys. Before joining the court, Toni practiced law for 16 years as a litigator at two Cleveland law firms and as in-house litigation counsel for Bridgestone Americas Holding, Inc. Toni was certified as an appellate law specialist by the Ohio State Bar Association in 2018. In her free time, Toni enjoys running, spending time with her boys, and listening to podcasts and audio books while walking her dogs.

[Brandon M. French, Staff Attorney](javascript:void(0))

Mr. French has been with the court since 2011. He received a Bachelor of Arts degree from The College of Wooster in 2007, and obtained his law degree from Ohio Northern University, Pettit College of Law in 2010.

Following admission to the bar, Mr. French served as a Judicial Attorney for the Honorable Frank D. Celebrezze, Jr. and the Honorable Eileen T. Gallagher. He was assigned to his present position in 2024.

[David F. Parchem, Staff Attorney](javascript:void(0))

Mr. Parchem has been with the court since 1990. He received his B.A., summa cum laude, and J.D. from the University of Notre Dame.

Following admission to the Bar in 1980, he was Law Clerk for District Court Judge John M. Manos, associate with the firm of Buckingham, Doolittle & Burroughs, associate with the firm of Ward, Marein and Gillette and in private practice.

[Andrew N. Rodak, Staff Attorney](javascript:void(0))

Mr. Rodak joined the court in 1987. He received his B.A. from Cleveland State University, and J.D. from the Cleveland-Marshall College of Law.

Following admission to the Bar, he was a Law Clerk for Common Pleas Court Judges Daniel O. Corrigan and David T. Matia, Law Clerk for Appellate Judge David T. Matia and, in 1994, was assigned his present position.

